From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:43:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: let debugfs list the T8132
 camera's portrait sizes

macOS offers 1328x1760 and 1080x1920 for the J604's camera, and every
frame it delivers, these included, reports a 2688x1738 sensor readout: it
enlarges the two portrait sizes slightly, about 1.02 and 1.11 times. Every
config 6 window the driver uses has fewer rows than they need, so the
driver, which never enlarges, does not offer them, and whether the T8132
firmware's scaler enlarges at all has not been measured.

Add a root-only debugfs file, upscale_probe, on the IMX958's wide config.
While it is set, both sizes are listed; a stream of one takes the largest
even crop of its shape from the selected wide window, centred, for the
scaler to enlarge, and logs that crop. Unset, the default, the formats and
every stream are as before. The call-size rule's source check moves to a
helper both crop rules share, unchanged.

tools/asahi/isp-upscale-probe-tests.py builds the driver's preset functions
on the host and checks the crops, the listing and the debugfs file, with
seventeen mutations.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
